exports[`git.grove.capacity given: [case1] a grove with a live behavior crew and an uncalibrated pool when: [t1] the read renders the tree then: the render, its live values masked, matches its snapshot 1`] = `
"🌲 grove capacity (token cost over N min)
   ├─ tokens, fleet-wide: N/h now
   │  ├─ per crew-hour: behavior N · directive ⚪
   │  ├─ 5h: ⚪ the cap ledger holds no rows — wire \`claude.statusline.caplog\` on each seat, then restart it
   │  └─ 7d: ⚪ the cap ledger holds no rows — wire \`claude.statusline.caplog\` on each seat, then restart it
   └─ grove local: N cpu · NG free of NG · N crews live, N at work · busy N of N · N forks/s (N per seat) · cpu stall ◯ N% (since boot N%) · ram full stall ◯ N% (since boot N%)
      ├─ behavior: affordable N (upper bound) · binds <axis> · free slots N · ram N · cpu N · tokens_Nh ⚪ · tokens_Nd ⚪
      ├─ directive: affordable N (upper bound) · binds <axis> · free slots N · ram N · cpu N · tokens_Nh ⚪ · tokens_Nd ⚪ · costs borrowed from the grove median
      └─ exchange: N directive ≈ N behavior (on <axis>) — ⚪ an estimate: a cost is borrowed, so this is no measure

🥥 next
   ├─ ask for a slot: rhx git.grove.capacity --grove <g> --for behavior --key <branch>
   ├─ rank the levers: rhx git.grove.capacity --levers
   └─ calibrate the caps: rhx git.crew.tokens calibrate
"
`;

